// D16953: a list of a union a pin mints (`(V | IM)[]` at `V := string`) stored into a record field
// the pin mints too. The list's rep exists only once the pin registers its union, after reps were
// first asked, so the rep tree is rebuilt for it.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
type IM = {[i32]: i32}
type R = { r: i32 }
function h<V>(x: IM): (V | IM)[] {
  const xs: (V | IM)[] = [x]
  const b: { v: (V | IM)[] } = { v: xs }
  return b.v
}
function seeded(): IM {
  const m: IM = Map()
  m[1] = 11
  return m
}
// @@VALUE@@
h<string>(seeded())
// @@TYPE@@
(string | IM)[]
// @@PROOF@@
const e = v[0]
if e is IM { print(e[1] ?? -1) } else { print(e) }
// @@WANT@@
11
// @@TEST@@
v.length == 1
// @@HIT@@
print(11)
// @@MISS@@
print(0)
// @@CELL_unread@@
// want: 0
function g<V>(x: IM) {
  const xs: (V | IM)[] = [x]
  const b: { v: (V | IM)[] } = { v: xs }
  return 0
}
print(g<string>(seeded()))
// @@CELL_record_member@@
// want: 1
function g<V>(x: R) {
  const xs: (V | R)[] = [x]
  const b: { v: (V | R)[] } = { v: xs }
  return b.v.length
}
print(g<string>({ r: 1 }))
// @@CELL_sibling_field@@
// want: 1
function g<V>(x: IM) {
  const xs: (V | IM)[] = [x]
  const b: { v: (V | IM)[], k: i32 } = { v: xs, k: 1 }
  return b.k
}
print(g<string>(seeded()))
// @@CELL_inferred_type_arg@@
// want: 1
function g<V>(y: V, x: IM) {
  const xs: (V | IM)[] = [x]
  const b: { v: (V | IM)[] } = { v: xs }
  return b.v.length
}
print(g("s", seeded()))
// @@CELL_two_pins@@
// want: 1 then 1
print(h<string>(seeded()).length)
print(h<boolean>(seeded()).length)
